{"title": "The Driven Podcast: Passing “Peak ICE,” BYD’s export armada, and the legacy price war", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/the-driven-podcast-passing-peak-ice-byds-export-armadas-and-the-legacy-price-war/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/the-driven-podcast-passing-peak-ice-byds-export-armadas-and-the-legacy-price-war/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"The Driven Podcast: Passing “Peak ICE,” BYD’s export armada, and the legacy price war\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/TD_Podcast_Cover_May26-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>We dig into the IEA's latest Global EV Outlook which says ICE vehicles peaked in 2017, BYD’s move to build its own export armada, and why legacy car makers are being dragged into a price war they may not be built to win.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/the-driven-podcast-passing-peak-ice-byds-export-armadas-and-the-legacy-price-war/\">The Driven Podcast: Passing “Peak ICE,” BYD’s export armada, and the legacy price war</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-21T18:28:20+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-23T07:26:09.646405+00:00"}
{"title": "“Cheaper to run:” Global EV numbers surge above 20 million despite slowdown in biggest markets", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/cheaper-to-run-global-ev-numbers-surge-above-20-million-despite-slowdown-in-biggest-markets/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/cheaper-to-run-global-ev-numbers-surge-above-20-million-despite-slowdown-in-biggest-markets/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"“Cheaper to run:” Global EV numbers surge above 20 million despite slowdown in biggest markets\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/petrol-ev-charging-nz-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Global oil shortages are driving more motorists to buy electric vehicles, with predictions they could account for almost one in three cars sold worldwide within a year.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/cheaper-to-run-global-ev-numbers-surge-above-20-million-despite-slowdown-in-biggest-markets/\">“Cheaper to run:” Global EV numbers surge above 20 million despite slowdown in biggest markets</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-21T15:16:55+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-23T07:26:09.646405+00:00"}
{"title": "Kia introduces innovative wheelchair accessible option to PV5 electric van", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/kia-introduces-innovative-wheelchair-accessible-option-to-pv5-electric-van/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/kia-introduces-innovative-wheelchair-accessible-option-to-pv5-electric-van/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Kia introduces innovative wheelchair accessible option to PV5 electric van\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/PV5-with-side-ramp-V3-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Retrofitting vehicles to make them wheelchair accessible always presents problems. Kia has found a solution - with a twist - for its new electric van.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/22/kia-introduces-innovative-wheelchair-accessible-option-to-pv5-electric-van/\">Kia introduces innovative wheelchair accessible option to PV5 electric van</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-21T15:14:11+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-23T07:26:09.646405+00:00"}
{"title": "Australian energy giant to roll out ultra-fast EV chargers at 7-Eleven stores", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/21/australian-energy-giant-to-roll-out-ultra-fast-ev-chargers-at-7-eleven-stores/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/21/australian-energy-giant-to-roll-out-ultra-fast-ev-chargers-at-7-eleven-stores/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australian energy giant to roll out ultra-fast EV chargers at 7-Eleven stores\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/EnergyAustralia-7-Eleven-ultra-fast-EV-charger-Roxburgh-Park-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>One of Australia’s three biggest privately owned energy utilities is rolling out 10 ultra-fast electric vehicle charging stations at 7-Eleven stores in Victoria, NSW and Queensland.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/21/australian-energy-giant-to-roll-out-ultra-fast-ev-chargers-at-7-eleven-stores/\">Australian energy giant to roll out ultra-fast EV chargers at 7-Eleven stores</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-20T21:10:25+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-23T07:26:09.646405+00:00"}
