{"title": "Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition\"><img alt=\"Incat 130m electric ferry\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Incat_02_small-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Electric ferries have gone from novelty to common sense in less than a decade. But Australian governments are still pretending the technology is stuck at the starting line?</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/\">Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T22:27:43+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-23T07:26:09.646405+00:00"}
